                The best rated mattress on Amazon depends on what you need, since ratings mix guest-room beds with primary beds. Among heavily reviewed models, the Nectar Classic is the strongest all-round foam bed, the Casper Original Hybrid the strongest hybrid, and the Zinus Green Tea and Linenspa hybrid the most popular budget beds. Read reviews from people with your sleep position and weight.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Is a mattress in a box as good as a store mattress?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                Often, yes. Many brands now sell the same construction in a box that they sell in stores, and a boxed bed usually costs less because it ships compressed. The difference is that you cannot try it first, so the trial period and return terms matter more. Allow up to 72 hours for it to expand fully before judging it.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">What firmness is best for a good mattress?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                Medium firm suits the largest number of people, especially back sleepers and combination sleepers. Side sleepers usually prefer medium or medium soft so the shoulder and hip can sink, and stomach sleepers usually prefer firm so the hips do not dip. Lighter people feel beds as firmer, heavier people as softer, so adjust the label to your weight.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Is a hybrid or memory foam mattress better?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                Neither is better for everyone. Memory foam contours closely and absorbs a partner's movement but can sleep warmer. A hybrid adds coils for bounce, airflow and edge support and is easier to move on. Choose foam for motion isolation, a hybrid if you run hot, change positions often or weigh more than average.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">How long does a mattress in a box last?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                Most last about seven to ten years, depending on foam density, coil type and the weight they carry. Budget all-foam beds tend to soften sooner; pocketed-coil hybrids and denser foams usually last longer. Rotating the bed every few months, using a proper base and keeping a protector on all help it reach the longer end of that range.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">How long does a new mattress smell last?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                The new-foam smell is strongest at unboxing and usually fades within a few days to two weeks. Serta, for example, advises one to two weeks to air out. Open windows, run a fan and leave the bed uncovered for the first day to speed it up. CertiPUR-US certified foams are tested for certain emissions.
              </p>
            </div>

